      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t this depend on depsets being ordered? That is, \"depset_i may only depend on depset_j if i \u003e j\" ? \n\n(For example, consider depset A depends on depset B, and depset B is empty. If A comes first, then B won\u0027t yet be present in emptyDepsetIds, thus we\u0027ll include B. Then, when B comes about, we\u0027ll omit it entirely. A will thus be unresolvable.)\n\nI\u0027m unclear on whether this ordering is a Bazel guarantee. (It might be the case today, but who knows in the future? unless it\u0027s a documented invariant)\n\nHowever, I believe we\u0027d immediately see a build failure if this invariant were broken -- ninja should complain immediately that it can\u0027t resolve the inputs of an action. \n\nIn the interest of getting this CL submitted quickly, I think it\u0027s fine to proceed with this implementation. However, we should either extensively document this assumed invariant (and a failure that might arise), or file a bug and fix this as a quick followup.",
